{"book":8,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"Gleaning in Boaz's Field","summary":"Ruth goes out to gather leftover grain and happens to work in the field of Boaz, a wealthy relative of Naomi's husband. Boaz protects and feeds her, and Naomi realizes he is one of their family's redeemers.","background":"God's law told farmers to leave the edges and leftovers of the harvest for the poor and the foreigner (Leviticus 19:9-10), so gleaning was Ruth's right. Boaz goes further, telling his workers to drop extra stalks for her (v. 16). By evening she has about an ephah of barley (v. 17), many days' food.","customs":[{"term":"One of our next kinsmen","verses":"2:20","note":"The Hebrew word is go'el, 'redeemer': a close relative responsible to help family in trouble, such as buying back land a relative had to sell (Leviticus 25:25)."}],"watchFor":["'Her hap was to light on a part of the field belonging unto Boaz' (v. 3).","Boaz prays she will be rewarded by the God 'under whose wings thou art come to trust' (v. 12).","Boaz invites a foreign gleaner to eat with his reapers (v. 14)."],"connections":["Leviticus 19:9-10","Leviticus 25:25","Deuteronomy 24:19","Psalms 91:4"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וּלְנָעֳמִי","uleno'omi","H5281","HC/R/Npf","and [belonged] to Naomi"],["מוֹדַע","meyuda'","H4129","HNcmsa","a relative"],["לְאִישָׁהּ","le'ishah","H376","HR/Ncmsc/Sp3fs","of husband her"],["אִישׁ","'ish","H376","HNcmsa","a man"],["גִּבּוֹר","gibor","H1368","HNcmsc","mighty of"],["חַיִל","chayil","H2428","HNcmsa","wealth"],["מִמִּשְׁפַּחַת","mimishpachat","H4940","HR/Ncfsc","from [the] clan of"],["אֱלִימֶלֶךְ","'elimelekh","H458","HNpm","Elimelech"],["וּשְׁמוֹ","ushemo","H8034","HC/Ncmsc/Sp3ms","and name his"],["בֹּעַז","bo'az","H1162","HNpm","[was] Boaz"]],"x":[[8004021,8004021,5],[8003002,8003002,4],[8003012,8003012,4],[40001005,40001005,3]],"xn":4},"2":{"w":[["וַתֹּאמֶר","vatomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3fs","and she said"],["רוּת","rut","H7327","HNpf","Ruth"],["הַמּוֹאֲבִיָּה","hamo'a